-- title:
--   A place with ordᵥ(jmath̃-c)>0 is the place jmath̃=c
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field. Write $\tilde{\jmath} =$ `jqModC k` for the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\,\eta^{-24})$ with coefficients reduced into $k$ (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, obtained from the integral power series `jNum` $= E_4^3\cdot$ `dedekindEtaUnitInv`), and let `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` be the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries k` over $k$ generated by $\tilde{\jmath}$ together with its level-one $q$-expansion rescaling, so that $\tilde{\jmath}$ lies in it by `jqModC_mem k 1`. Let $v$ be a place of this field over $k$ in the project's sense, i.e. a valuation subring of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` that contains the image of $k$, is not the whole field, and is a principal ideal ring, and let `v.ord` be the associated integer-valued order function. Let $c \in k$. The assertion is: if $\operatorname{ord}_v\bigl(\tilde{\jmath} - c\bigr) > 0$, where $c$ is viewed in the field through the structure map of $k$, then $v$ equals `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k c`, the place obtained by transporting the finite place of $k(t)$ attached to the irreducible polynomial $t - c$ along the $k$-algebra isomorphism $k(t) \xrightarrow{\sim}$ `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` sending $t \mapsto \tilde{\jmath}$. No hypothesis is imposed on $k$ beyond being a field.
--
--   This is the level-one place-pinning statement for the $j$-line: a place of the modular function field of level one at which the function $\tilde{\jmath} - c$ has strictly positive order is exactly the place centred at the moduli point $\tilde{\jmath} = c$. It is used in the analysis of specialisations of places on modular curves, for instance when identifying the reduction of a place centred at an integral value of $j$ and in the Cerednik–Drinfeld comparison of class sets with sets of places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_eq_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_of_ord_pos.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_SpecializeModuli

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve ModularCurve

theorem ModularCurve.eq_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_of_ord_pos
    {k : Type*} [Field k] {v : Place k ↥(modularFunctionFieldC k 1)} {c : k}
    (h : 0 < v.ord ((⟨jqModC k, jqModC_mem k 1⟩ : modularFunctionFieldC k 1)
      - algebraMap k (modularFunctionFieldC k 1) c)) :
    v = charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k c := by sorry
